# --- Generated data & runtime output ---
# Batches are regenerated from a seed; the seed is the source of truth, not the CSVs.
# Generated batches, anywhere in the tree — `data/*` alone only matches the root.
# Batches are reproducible from a seed, so the seed is the artefact worth keeping,
# not several megabytes of CSV.
/data/*
!/data/.gitkeep
engine/data/
# Blind-test batches and their answer keys. Never committed: a committed answer
# key is not an answer key.
data/blind/
finctl-answers/
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.db
audit/*.jsonl
# Coverage output is a measurement of a run, not an artefact of the project. The
# number belongs in METRICS.md; the binary does not belong in git.
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/

# --- Design handoff archives ---
# The exported zip from the design tool. Its CONTENTS are adopted into web/ and
# committed there; the archive itself is a several-megabyte duplicate of work that
# already lives in the tree as code.
*handoff*.zip

# --- Buildathon-internal process docs: not product documentation ---
/PROJECT-CONTEXT.md
/build-plan-3.5-days.md
/docs/DEMO-SCRIPT.md

# --- OS / editor ---
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
